<title>POLAND: KPW clears Polish Biurosystem for public trade.</title>
<headline>KPW clears Polish Biurosystem for public trade.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Securities Commission has cleared for public trade the initial public offering of Polish office equipment firm Biurosystem SA, the KPW said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>The firm's 265,600 existing shares have also been approved for trade.</p>
<p>No of Shares Offered: 434,400</p>
<p> Tranches		  No Of Shares	   Subscription</p>
<p>			     Offered		  Period</p>
<p> Large-investor	  300,000		  July 21-24</p>
<p> Small-investor	   75,700		  July 14-18</p>
<p> Employee tranche	 58,700		  July 14-18</p>
<p> Lead Manager:	   BOS brokerage</p>
<p> Price*:		   20-25/shr</p>
<p> Lead Underwriter:     BOS</p>
<p> Use Of Proceeds:	investments in expanding the firm's</p>
<p>			     trade network</p>
<p>Note: * - price as estimated by the firm. The company seeks a parallel market listing.</p>
<p> EARNINGS DATA	   1996		    1995</p>
<p>(in million of PLN)</p>
<p> Net profit:	     0.06		    0.27</p>
<p> Sales:		   21.27		   18.13</p>
<p>No of existing shares: 265,600 None of the company's shareholders has a stake of more that 10 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
